{"id": "54:4", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "declinavérunt in me iniquitátes", "portuguese": "voltaram iniquidades contra mim", "problem": "The Portuguese rightly keeps the Latin's ambiguity: 'iniquitates' can be the subject ('iniquities bent upon me') or the object ('they turned iniquities upon me', as in the LXX ἐξέκλιναν ἐπ' ἐμὲ ἀνομίαν). But 'voltaram' most readily means 'returned', which is a sense the Latin does not have. 'declinare in' means to bend or turn aside onto, not to come back.", "fix": "Porque declinaram iniquidades sobre mim"}]},
{"id": "54:10", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "contradictiónem", "portuguese": "a contenda", "problem": "'contradictio' means gainsaying or speaking against (LXX ἀντιλογίαν). 'contenda' (strife) is broader and less exact.", "fix": "porque vi a iniquidade e a contradição na cidade."}]},
{"id": "54:15", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "ambulávimus", "portuguese": "andávamos", "problem": "The Latin has the perfect here, set against the imperfect 'capiebas' in the first half-verse. The Portuguese makes both imperfect and loses the change of tense.", "fix": "na casa de Deus andamos em concórdia."}]},
{"id": "54:20b", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "in retribuéndo", "portuguese": "para retribuir", "problem": "'in' + ablative gerund means 'in the act of repaying' (LXX ἐν τῷ ἀποδιδόναι). It does not express purpose, so 'para' turns it into a purpose clause.", "fix": "estendeu a sua mão ao retribuir."}]}
],
"overall": "The translation is faithful and close throughout. It keeps the Septuagintal readings (exercitatio, pusillanimitas, 'super oleum', 'non dimidiabunt'), the ejus/illius distinction in 54:21, and the Latin's ambiguities, such as 'inter multos erant mecum'. The faults are minor: one misleading verb in 54:4, one lexical choice in 54:10, and one small tense or construction slip each in 54:15 and 54:20b. Every verse has one mediant, matching the Latin, and there are no flexes on either side."}
